    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The number $2a$ has exactly 10 divisors, and the number $3a$ has exactly 6 divisors. Find the sum of the first and last digits of the number $2019a$.",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "13"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "Impossible to determine"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Divisor-count formula",
        "body": "Write $a=2^x3^ym$ with $m$ coprime to 6. Then\n$$d(2a)=(x+2)(y+1)\\,d(m)=10,\\qquad d(3a)=(x+1)(y+2)\\,d(m)=6.$$\n$d(m)$ divides both 10 and 6, so $d(m)\\in\\{1,2\\}$.\n\n- $d(m)=2$: $(x+2)(y+1)=5$ forces $x=3$, $y=0$, but then $(x+1)(y+2)=8\\ne3$.\n- $d(m)=1$ ($m=1$): $(x+2)(y+1)=10$ with $x+2\\ge2$: $(x,y)=(0,4)$, $(3,1)$ or $(8,0)$. Only $(0,4)$ gives $(x+1)(y+2)=6$.\n\nSo $a=3^4=81$ (check: $162=2\\cdot3^4$ has $2\\cdot5=10$ divisors, $243=3^5$ has 6). Then $2019\\cdot81 = 163539$, and $1+9=10$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 10**"
      }
    ],
