        "text": "Another answer"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use $R=\\frac{abc}{4\\,\\text{Area}}$",
        "body": "Let the side be 3, $M$ the midpoint of $BC$. The height is $AM=\\frac{3\\sqrt3}2$, and $K,L$ are at distance $\\frac12$ from $M$. So $KL=1$ and $AK=AL=\\sqrt{\\frac14+\\frac{27}4}=\\sqrt7$.\n\nArea of $AKL$ $=\\frac12\\cdot1\\cdot\\frac{3\\sqrt3}2=\\frac{3\\sqrt3}4$, so\n$$R_{AKL}=\\frac{\\sqrt7\\cdot\\sqrt7\\cdot1}{4\\cdot\\frac{3\\sqrt3}4}=\\frac7{3\\sqrt3}.$$\nFor $ABC$: $R=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt3}=\\sqrt3$. Ratio $\\frac{7}{3\\sqrt3}:\\sqrt3 = 7:9$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 7:9**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Law of sines",
        "body": "In triangle $AKL$ the angle at $K$ satisfies $\\sin\\angle AKL=\\frac{AM}{AK}=\\frac{3\\sqrt3/2}{\\sqrt7}$, and the opposite side is $AL=\\sqrt7$. So $2R_{AKL}=\\frac{AL}{\\sin K}=\\frac{7\\cdot 2}{3\\sqrt3}$. For $ABC$: $2R=\\frac{3}{\\sin60^\\circ}=2\\sqrt3$. Ratio $\\frac{14/(3\\sqrt3)}{2\\sqrt3}=\\frac79$.\n\n**Answer: (B)**"
      }
    ],
